04-02T05:33:00Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116718","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116718","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116718.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116718.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Removes unnecessary mutex locks from functions where they are not required. I figure most of these are remnants from when `RID_Owner` was not thread safe.\r\n\r\nI also fixed a few race conditions that I noticed:\r\n- Draw list can read framebuffer formats map while it is getting written in a different thread. I don't practically see this happening since framebuffers always get created on the render thread, but it is technically allowed.\r\n- Pipeline creation and draw list can read vertex formats map while it is getting written in a different thread. This realistically CAN happen.\r\n\r\nEventually I'd like to completely get rid of `_THREAD_SAFE_METHOD_` and use multiple mutexes. This would allow `vertex_array_create`/`index_array_create`/`uniform_set_create` functions to run in parallel and not throttle unrelated rendering functions. However, it is much more complicated than it sounds due to how draw trackers are managed.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116718/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116718/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}